      },
      {
        "number": 2,
        "text": "Ann's Key Lime Pie\n\n1 prepared graham cracker pie crust\n1 package (8 oz) cream cheese, softened\n1 can (14 oz) sweetened condensed milk (not evaporated)\n1 cup evaporated milk\n1/2 cup lime juice\nGrated peel of 1 small lime\n\nPreheat oven to 375°. Brush pie crust with egg white and bake for 5 minutes, or until browned.\nIn a small mixer bowl, beat cream cheese until smooth. Gradually add sweetened condensed milk and evaporated milk. Beat until smooth. With mixer on medium speed, add lime juice and grated peel, mixing until smooth.\nPour into pie crust and freeze for at least 2 hours. Let stand at room temperature 10 to 15 minutes before serving. (over)",
        "method": "vision",
        "decoration_text": [],
        "uncertain": [
          "Ann's"
        ],
